title: ' [Release|CI/CD] prdoc: make the changelog topic field usable by contributors'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Closes: https://github.com/paritytech/release-engineering/issues/300

    Part of paritytech/polkadot-sdk#6424

    Makes the optional prdoc `topic` override discoverable and safe to use. Now `topic` can be added (if needed) in three ways:
    1. Auto generated based on the schema
    2. Directly in the .prdoc file using `topic` field
    3. Bu using `cmd-bot`: `/cmd prdoc --topic <id>` with the reason posted back on failure

    Also added:
    - docs in schema, template and docs;
    - soft validation in `check-prdoc.py` (warning, never a failure);
    - unknown values are a notice in the changelog generator (and its CI job summary) instead of a  failed --check.

    Topic matching lives in one place (`match_topic` in generate.py, shared via .github/scripts/prdoc_topics.py), with `aliases` for legacy values.
crates: []
topic: bogus
